+### 5.9 session_list
+
+The server answers a valid `list_sessions` request with one `session_list` frame for the socket's authenticated user. Each summary contains only `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`; both times are ISO-8601 strings on the wire. The server forwards `limit` and `before` to `SessionStore.listFor` and ignores a client-supplied `userId` ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L96)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "session_list",
+  "sessions": [
+    {
+      "sessionId": "s1",
+      "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
+      "updatedAt": "2026-01-02T00:00:00.000Z",
+      "entryCount": 2
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field                   | Type     | Description                                    |
+| ----------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                  | string   | `"session_list"`                               |
+| `sessions`              | object[] | Conversation summaries in store list order     |
+| `sessions[].sessionId`  | string   | Id to use with `?sessionId=` when reconnecting |
+| `sessions[].createdAt`  | string   | Creation time as an ISO-8601 string            |
+| `sessions[].updatedAt`  | string   | Last activity time as an ISO-8601 string       |
+| `sessions[].entryCount` | number   | Number of entries in the conversation          |
+
+If the store has no `listFor`, the server answers an empty `session_list`; a throwing `listFor` produces `SERVER_ERROR` and a `ws` error log ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L137)).
+
